[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Pirc Defence"]
[Variation "Pirc Defence: 150 Attack"]
[ECO "B07"]
[Character "positional,sharp"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "150-attack,h-pawn-storm"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 d6 (1... g6 2. d4 { Same plan against the Modern move order: build the centre first and let Black's pieces come to it. } 2... Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be3 Nf6 5. Qd2) 2. d4 { Takes the centre while Black has not challenged it. Two pawns side by side give White space and Black's pieces less room. } 2... Nf6 3. Nc3 { Defends e4, which the knight on f6 attacks, and develops a piece. } 3... g6 4. Be3 { Brings the bishop out before the queen. With Qd2 and Bh6 next, this is the "150 Attack", a plan that works against almost every Pirc setup. } 4... Bg7
5. Qd2 { Protects the bishop on e3 and prepares Bh6 to swap off Black's strong g7 bishop, the main guard of Black's king. } 5... O-O 6. f3 { Holds e4 with a pawn so the knight on c3 is free to move, and gives the king's side a solid shape before the attack starts. } 6... c6 (6... Nc6 7. Nge2 { Develops the last knight without blocking the f-pawn, and keeps d4 guarded. }) 7. Bh6 { Offers to swap bishops. Without the g7 bishop Black's king has few defenders, and White's queen lands on h6 beside it. } 7... Bxh6 (7... e5 8. Bxg7 Kxg7 9. O-O-O { Castling long puts the king away from the pawn storm and the rook on the open d-file. })
8. Qxh6 { The queen now sits next to the king and supports the h-pawn push. } 8... Nbd7 9. h4 { Starts the pawn storm: the h-pawn will reach h5 and open the h-file against the king. } 9... b5 10. h5 { Plan: keep pushing the h-pawn, develop Nge2 and castle long, then open the h-file. If Black strikes in the centre with ...e5, keep d4 and e4 protected before you attack. } *
